# Line endings are stored as LF whatever platform a file was edited on.
#
# Not a style preference. This repo contains bash — inside the `run:` blocks of
# the workflows in .github/workflows/ and in scripts/test-reset-workflow.sh — and
# a carriage return in front of a line ending is a syntax error to bash, not a
# line ending. A workflow committed from Windows with CRLF fails at run time with
# something like `syntax error near unexpected token`, which points at the shell
# rather than at the line ending that caused it.
#
# `text=auto` leaves genuinely binary files — the images and video under
# public/media — alone; git works that out from the file's own contents rather
# than from its name.
* text=auto eol=lf